    LLM: 'Game: 3 5 7 Poker. Three stages, declare in/out each; only player in scores a leg or showdown with match pot. First to three legs wins.',
    Player: 'Three-stage Guts: 3 then 5 then 7 cards; threes, fives, sevens wild by stage. Declare in or out each stage; first to three legs wins the pot.',
    objective: 'Be the first to collect three legs: either be the only player to stay in at a stage (score one leg) or win a showdown when multiple stay in (losers match the pot); first to three legs wins the entire pot.',
    gameplay: 'Three stages. Stage one: all ante, three cards dealt face down to each player; players declare in or out (sequence or simultaneous). If one stays in they score a leg; if two or more stay in they compare hands (triplets beat pairs beat nothing; threes wild), loser(s) pay pot to winner(s). Stage two: two more cards dealt (five total); fives wild; best five-card poker hand wins among those in; same payment rule. Stage three: two more cards (seven total); sevens wild; best five-card from seven wins; same rule. If no one has three legs, everyone antes again and redeal from three cards. First to three legs takes the pot.',
